@@ -2,6 +2,28 @@

 JSON in, JSON out. Routes are listed in `README.md`.

+## Authentication
+
+Send `Authorization: Bearer <key>` on every request. Add your keys to the
+`apiKeys` array of the configured data file before starting the server.
+Each entry has a unique `key`, a `name` used in the audit log, and a `role`.
+The keys in `data/seed.json` are public examples for local testing.
+
+- `viewer` can use GET routes other than `GET /audit`.
+- `cook` has viewer permissions plus `POST /recipes/:id/cook`,
+  `POST /batches/:id/waste`, `POST /temperatures`, and
+  `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`.
+- `manager` can use every route.
+
+Missing or unknown keys return 401 (`unauthorized`). A key with
+insufficient permissions returns 403 (`forbidden`).
+
+## Audit route
+
+`GET /audit` returns audit entries newest first and requires a manager key.
+Each successful write records `time` (UTC ISO 8601), `keyName`, `method`,
+`path` (the URL pathname), and `status` (the HTTP response status).
+
 ## Errors

 Errors have a status from `src/errors.js` and the body
